DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The vvffss__ggeettvvffss() function returns the mount point structure for a file
     system given its file system identifier.  The file system ID should have
     been allocated by calling vfs_getnewfsid(9); otherwise, it will not be
     found.

     A major user of vvffss__ggeettvvffss() is NFS, which uses the _f_s_i_d as part of file
     handles in order to determine the file system a given RPC is for.  If
     vvffss__ggeettvvffss() fails to find the mount point related to _f_s_i_d, the file sys‐
     tem is considered stale.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     If _f_s_i_d is found, the mount point for the ID is returned; otherwise, NULL
     is returned.

